-- Farbaek schema v56: browsers' roles get back exactly what the migrations
-- give them (ADR 0088).
--
-- Production was restored at some point without its privileges, so every
-- table and function that existed then took Supabase's default "grant all"
-- for anon and authenticated, including the app_* functions only the server
-- may call. Row Level Security kept rows apart, but the functions trust the
-- actor they're given. This sets every table, column, sequence and function
-- in public and private to the state the migrations before it define,
-- generated by scripts/ops/browser-grants.mjs. Where the privileges are
-- already right, as in a fresh database, it changes nothing.

revoke all on all tables in schema public from anon, authenticated;
revoke all on all sequences in schema public from anon, authenticated;
